Given the actual figure, the caption should use its “real path” and “branch path” terminology:

**Figure 1: Logit-shift distillation.** At position (t), the draft model proposes (a_t=\textit{puppy}), whereas the target model prefers (x_t=\textit{dog}). Because (a_t) remains within the target’s top-(k) candidates, it forms a plausible alternative branch. Both the target and draft models are evaluated along the real path (x_1,\ldots,x_t) and the branch path (x_1,\ldots,a_t). For each model, the difference between the centered branch-path and real-path logits defines its logit shift. The objective matches the draft’s shift (\Delta_D) to the target’s shift (\Delta_T), directly supervising how the next-token distribution changes after a plausible alternative token is introduced.

